# Terraform Secure Baseline v1.9.0

## Finished v1.9.0 Criteria

One canonical ecs_services map.

scaling = null means no platform-owned autoscaling target/policy.

Registered-but-unreleased services create no ECS scaling resources.

Fixed services:
Terraform owns desired_count.

Autoscaled services:
desired_count is bootstrap capacity;
Application Auto Scaling owns subsequent desired count.

Never let Terraform reassert the bootstrap count after an autoscaler
has legitimately changed it.

Application Auto Scaling policies use target tracking only in v1.9.

ALBRequestCountPerTarget requires ingress.

The ALB scaling resource label comes from Terraform-owned resource
identities, not string reconstruction in Bash.

AWS-managed target-tracking CloudWatch alarms remain AWS-managed.
Do not edit or repurpose them.

Operational notification alarms are separate Terraform-owned alarms.

ECS autoscaling remains workload-baseline infrastructure.

No fifth validation/evidence layer.

Keep the existing ECS/ECR/ALB/cluster module boundaries.

Keep private Fargate / assign_public_ip = false.

Keep digest-pinned application releases.

Deploy Application continues to change only image_digest.
It does not manage service scaling configuration.

The exact-saved-plan Apply workflow remains unchanged.

## Roadmap

| Milestone                             | Purpose                                                                                                                                                            | Expected repository areas                                                                                                                                     |
| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **O1 — Scaling Ownership & Contract** | Finalize canonical scaling schema; prove fixed-vs-autoscaled `desired_count` ownership and safe state transition with plans only/test state before production code | `docs/ecs-runtime-design.md`, `baseline/variables.tf`, `modules/ecs_service/`, possibly migration documentation/tooling                                       |
| **O2 — Core ECS Auto Scaling**        | Application Auto Scaling target plus CPU/memory target-tracking policies; resource-backed outputs                                                                  | `modules/ecs_service/main.tf`, `variables.tf`, `outputs.tf`, `baseline/locals.tf`, `baseline/main.tf`, `baseline/outputs.tf`, environment variable interfaces |
| **O3 — ALB Request Scaling**          | Add `ALBRequestCountPerTarget`; derive exact resource label from ALB/TG resources                                                                                  | `modules/application_load_balancer/outputs.tf`, `modules/ecs_service/`, `baseline/locals.tf`                                                                  |
| **O4 — Deployment Health**            | Minimum healthy %, maximum %, health-check grace; preserve current defaults when absent                                                                            | `modules/ecs_service/variables.tf`, `main.tf`, outputs, canonical `ecs_services` interface                                                                    |
| **O5 — Operational Signals**          | Task-deficit and ingress health alarms; optional CPU/memory/5xx alerts; reuse notification architecture                                                            | `modules/monitoring/variables.tf`, `main.tf`, outputs, `baseline/main.tf`, `baseline/locals.tf`                                                               |
| **O6 — Exact Runtime Validation**     | Extend existing ECS validator for scaling targets, policies, deployment settings, dynamic count semantics, and alarm state                                         | `scripts/validation/validate-ecs-runtime.sh`, `scripts/validation/README.md`, `docs/validation-checklist.md`; baseline output contracts                       |
| **O7 — Live Qualification & Release** | Exercise scale-out/in, releases while scaled, alarms, full evidence, docs, no-change plan, then release                                                            | test fixtures, `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/ecs-runtime-design.md`, deployment docs if needed                                                           |

